/* =============================================================================
   composites.stanfunctions
   -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Composite-index construction functions for observed-variable Bayesian SEM and
   path-analysis models.

   Philosophy
   ----------
   Rather than estimating latent variables directly through CFA/SEM, this
   project constructs interpretable observed composites from standardized
   indicators. This improves:
     - model stability
     - interpretability
     - computational robustness
     - identifiability

   All composites are deterministic transformations of observed data.

   Core principles
   ---------------
     * Indicators are standardized before combination.
     * Composite directionality is harmonized so larger values consistently
       represent "more" of the construct.
     * Equal weighting is used by default to minimize researcher degrees of
       freedom and avoid overfitting.
     * Composite construction is pre-specified before outcome modeling.

   Functions
   ---------

     composite(items, sign)
       Builds an equal-weight additive composite index from a matrix of items.

       Inputs:
         items : N x J matrix of indicators
         sign  : vector of +1 / -1 values controlling direction alignment

       Procedure:
         1. Standardize each indicator
         2. Reverse-code indicators where sign[j] = -1
         3. Average standardized indicators equally

       Output:
         Composite score on an approximately standardized scale.

       Typical use:
         - metabolic burden indices
         - self-care indices
         - diet quality indices
         - barrier/friction indices

     activity_index(intensity, duration, frequency)
       Builds a MET-style physical activity composite inspired by standard
       metabolic-equivalent formulations.

       Inputs:
         intensity : activity intensity measure
         duration  : activity duration measure
         frequency : activity frequency measure

       Procedure:
         1. Apply log1p transform to stabilize skewed count-like scales
         2. Standardize each component
         3. Compute equal-weight additive activity score

       Motivation
       ----------
       Classical MET formulations are based on combinations of:
           intensity × duration × frequency

       This implementation provides a stabilized and standardized proxy suitable
       for regression and mediation modeling.

   Typical usage
   -------------
       #include "lib/composites.stanfunctions"

   Dependencies
   ------------
     Requires:
       zscore() from utils.stanfunctions

   ============================================================================= */
// Build an equal-weight composite from a block of items with per-item signs.
vector composite(matrix items, vector sign) {
    int N = rows(items);
    int J = cols(items);
    vector[N] acc = rep_vector(0, N);
    for (j in 1:J) acc += sign[j] * zscore(items[, j]);
    return acc / J;
}

// MET proxy: intensity (level) x duration (time) x frequency (sessions/wk).
// Product matches the study's MET computation; single log tames right-skew.
vector activity_index(
    vector intensity,
    vector duration,
    vector frequency
) {
    int N = rows(intensity);
    vector[N] mets = intensity .* duration .* frequency;  // elementwise PRODUCT
    return zscore(log1p(mets));                            // single log, then z
}